# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The encode isolated: 1M-row table in the benchmark's shape, 100k-row batches,
# ring.next (fetch + columnar_build + publish) against ring.next_rows (the row
# frame, which does no transpose) as the control. Same script both images.
#
# command:
#   flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
#       -v /tmp/opencode/encode_probe.py:/tmp/encode_probe.py:ro \
#       fpq-baseline|fpq-databases python3 /tmp/encode_probe.py <label>'
#
# baseline (three interleaved runs):
baseline-1: columnar next 112.62 ns/row median, min 108.07, max 191.88, n=50
baseline-1: rows next 34.12 ns/row median, min 33.38, max 38.99, n=50
baseline-2: columnar next 113.95 ns/row median, min 109.56, max 193.13, n=50
baseline-2: rows next 34.64 ns/row median, min 33.57, max 40.12, n=50
baseline-3: columnar next 110.35 ns/row median, min 107.43, max 175.14, n=50
baseline-3: rows next 34.20 ns/row median, min 33.52, max 38.84, n=50
#
# change (three interleaved runs):
databases-1: columnar next 103.52 ns/row median, min 99.21, max 225.38, n=50
databases-1: rows next 34.29 ns/row median, min 33.57, max 43.56, n=50
databases-2: columnar next 101.99 ns/row median, min 97.69, max 166.72, n=50
databases-2: rows next 34.01 ns/row median, min 33.26, max 38.81, n=50
databases-3: columnar next 106.41 ns/row median, min 103.17, max 174.90, n=50
databases-3: rows next 34.18 ns/row median, min 33.43, max 37.77, n=50
#
# wire identity: sha256 over every exposed frame byte (names/kinds/types, data,
# offsets+bytes, null bitmaps) is identical on baseline and change for the bench,
# NULL-heavy, growing-text-retry and binary-kind shapes. See DESIGN.md.

### AB
benchmarks.sh 100000: stream() 8.27M -> 9.37M rows/s (+13.3%), PATHS stream 8.19M -> 9.41M (+14.9%); encode isolation: ring.next columnar 112.6 -> 103.5 ns/row median (-8.1%, the row-frame control is flat 34.2 -> 34.2); tests.sh green (55 client tests + make installcheck).
